-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",66,{
[2081]="700000F5\n1\tDrukordh can be found in the deepest, most southern recesses of Nan Wathren. Gildor told you that if the Uruk Drukordh were slain, then Lin Giliath would remain safe enough for him to come to the Council of Esteldín. You were warned not to confront the Uruk without the help of allies. Using the Elf-stone allows you to access the inspiration buff while solo or in a smaller fellowship.\t\n2\tReturn to Gildor at Lin Giliath\tGildor can be found in Lin Giliath. With the Uruk Drukordh slain, you should make your way back to Gildor and bring him this good news.\n",
[2082]="700000F6\n1\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad can be found in Esteldín. Gildor told you to bring word to Halbarad that the Elves have agreed to come to the Council of Esteldín.\n",
[2083]="70042DCF\n1\tFind the secret ferry among the reeds in the eastern reaches of Lossarnach\tA friend of Gondor operates a secret ferry across the river among the reeds that border the Anduin, on the eastern side of Lossarnach. Angbor has asked you to enter Ithilien by yourself while he seeks to assail the Harlond with his army.\n2\tTalk to the secret ferrywoman\tA friend of Gondor operates a secret ferry across the river among the reeds that border the Anduin, on the eastern side of Lossarnach. Angbor has asked you to enter Ithilien by yourself while he seeks to assail the Harlond with his army.\n3\tDefeat Haradrim in South Ithilien (total: 10)\tYou have been given permission to cross into Ithilien and seek Faramir's Rangers at Bâr Húrin, as long as you defeat Haradrim in those woods as you go.\n4\tFind the camp of Faramir's Rangers at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien\tYou have crossed into Ithilien and seek Faramir's Rangers at Bâr Húrin.\n5\tTalk to Duilin at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien\tDuilin is at the camp of Faramir's Rangers, at Bâr Húrin in South Ithilien. Duilin of the Blackroot Vale has called your name and beckoned you to speak to him.\n",
[2084]="70061C33\n1\tTalk to Meneldir at Sarn Ford\tMeneldir is at Sarn Ford. Meneldir is eager to set forth in search of his scattered kin.\n2\tSearch for scattered Rangers at an Elf-camp across the river\tElves camp east of the river near Caranost. Meneldir believes that some of the scattered Rangers likely made their way for one of the Elf-camps across the river from Caranost.\n3\tTalk to Handarod at Sírlond\tHandarod rallies the Rangers at Sírlond, an Elf-camp across the river from Caranost, the old capital of Cardolan.\n4\tDefeat foes in the South Downs that endanger the scattered Rangers (total: 12)\tDangerous foes stalk the South Downs, making it difficult for scattered kinfolk of the Ranger Handarod to make it to Sírlond. He has asked you to do what you can to help.\n5\tTalk to Handarod at Sírlond\tRanger Handarod is at Sírlond, waiting for word of your success in the South Downs.\n6\tFind the Rangers that made for Scurloc Farm, to the north-east of Caranost\tHandarod believes other Rangers gather at Scurloc Farm, to the north-east.\n7\tTalk to Malenfang at Scurloc Farm\tRanger Malenfang watches over Scurloc Farm, in the South Downs.\n",
[2085]="70000102\n1\tTalk to Nellie Boskins\tNellie Boskins can be found in Trestlebridge. Halbarad warned you that Nellie may be so consumed with the defence of Trestlebridge that she will not see the importance of coming to the Council of Esteldín.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad can be found in Esteldín. Upon hearing your message regarding the Council of Esteldín, Nellie Boskins ardently refused to come, saying that the defence of her town was above all other concerns. You should return to Halbarad with her answer.\n",
[2086]="70000100\n1\tTalk to Halbarad\tTravel with Halbarad to Trestlebridge and aid in its defence. Halbarad told you that the Orcs moving on Trestlebridge are from the more powerful Ongbúrz tribe. The townsfolk will not be able to defend against them alone. Halbarad instructed you to gather allies and return to him. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Nellie Boskins\tNellie Boskins can be found in Trestlebridge. At Halbarad's side, you helped defend Trestlebridge from the Orcs that sought to destroy it. At the conclusion of the battle, Nellie Boskins asked to speak with you.\n",
[2087]="70000101\n1\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad can be found in Esteldín. Nellie Boskins has asked you to inform Halbarad that she will come to the Council of Esteldín.\n",
[2088]="70061C76\n1\tDefeat half-orcs at Amon Firn and find any orders they might be carrying\tHalf-orcs can be found near Amon Firn, in the South Downs. Malenfang has asked you to search for any orders the half-orcs might be carrying.\n2\tRead the half-orc orders\tYou should read the scrap of parchment you found on the half-orc's body.\n3\tBring the half-orc orders to Malenfang at Scurloc Farm\tMalenfang is at Scurloc Farm, waiting to see any of the half-orc orders you might have recovered.\n4\tSearch Haudh Nirui for scraps of orders to the goblins (total: 6)\tMalenfang believes that you might find more information about the shared purpose of the half-orcs and the goblins at the ruins of Haudh Nirui, north-west of Amon Firn.\n5\tSet the scraps of the orders on the table at Scurloc Farm\tThe orders you recovered have been torn to scraps by the goblins of Haudh Nirui, and will need to be properly sorted and reconstructed before they can be read.\n6\tSort the papers on the table at Scurloc Farm\tThe table at Scurloc Farm will serve as a good place to sort the scraps of the orders you recovered.\n7\tSort the papers on the table at Scurloc Farm\tThe table at Scurloc Farm will serve as a good place to sort the scraps of the orders you recovered.\n8\tSort the papers on the table at Scurloc Farm\tThe table at Scurloc Farm will serve as a good place to sort the scraps of the orders you recovered.\n9\tExamine the reconstructed orders on the table at Scurloc Farm\tYou have reassembled the scraps of the orders to the half-orcs and goblins of the South Downs, putting them into a readable form that seems to make sense.\n10\tTalk to Meneldir at Scurloc Farm about what you have learned\tMeneldir has arrived, and will want to see the orders you reconstructed.\n",
[2089]="70042DE0\n1\tTalk to Duilin and hunt the mighty Mûmakil\tDuilin is at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien. You have grudgingly agreed to help Duilin and Derufin hunt the mighty Mûmakil, in return for their help finding Faramir.\n2\tTalk to Duilin at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien\tDuilin is at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien. The Mûmak hunt did not go as planned, but Duilin and Derufin do not seem to mind.\n",
[2090]="70042DEB\n1\tFind Faramir or his men within the Osgiliath Culverts\tFaramir and his men may be found within the Osgiliath Culverts beneath the city, if they still stand against the armies of the enemy.\n2\tTalk to Damrod among the Osgiliath Culverts\tDamrod and the few Gondorian soldiers that still defend Osgiliath can be found among the culverts beneath the city.\n3\tDefeat Orcs throughout Osgiliath (total: 10)\030Search the south-western area of Osgiliath for one of Damrod's men\tOrcs can be found throughout Osgiliath, and Damrod hopes that you might find Faramir or soldiers with news of him in the south-western area of the city.\n4\tDefeat Orcs throughout Osgiliath (total: 8)\030Search the north-western area of Osgiliath for another of Damrod's men\tInthol told you that he last saw Faramir and Gelnor racing to the north-west area of Osgiliath, pursued by a frightful commander of the enemy forces named Gothmog.\n5\tGelnor saw an Orc runner crushed beneath falling stones near a fountain to the east, and he wants you to dig through the rubble in search of the message it carried.\t\n6\tMaybe you missed something. Keep digging! ([see journal]/3)\tGelnor saw an Orc runner crushed beneath falling stones near a fountain to the east, and he wants you to dig through the rubble in search of the message it carried.\n7\tBring the Orc-message to Damrod among the Osgiliath Culverts\tYou have recovered one of the messages sent by Gothmog to his forces in Osgiliath, and should bring it to Damrod among the culverts beneath the city.\n",
[2091]="70061C89\n1\tTalk to Malenfang at Scurloc Farm\tMalenfang is at Scurloc Farm, waiting to hear what you learned from the papers you deciphered.\n2\tTalk to Handarod at Sírlond\tHandarod is at Sírlond, across the river from Caranost, and he may know someone who might be able to tell you about the Grey Fear.\n3\tFind the hiding spot for Narndir's journal in a hollow place beneath the easternmost tower of Caranost\030Search the hiding spot for Narndir's journal\tNarndir kept his journals at a secret place in the South Downs, but Handarod was trusted with its location. The hiding spot is beneath one of the eastern towers of Caranost, in a hollow place beneath the tower.\n4\tRead Narndir's journal\tYou have recovered Narndir's journal, in which he recorded many thoughts about the history of Arnor and the kingdoms that followed after.\n5\tRead Narndir's journal while in the throne room of Caranost, located at the highest point of the ruined capital of Cardolan\tNarndir's journal describes the throne room of Caranost, located at the highest point of the ruined city. You should travel to the location described by the journal, and read the appropriate pages while you are there.\n6\tConsider the image of King Tarondor II\tNarndir's writing is so evocative you can almost imagine King Tarondor II is present in the throne room he established at Caranost following the breaking of Arnor.\n7\tRead Narndir's journal while near the top of Amon Firn, by climbing the path located on the north side of the hill\tNarndir's journal contains an account of the Battle of the Deadmount, and describes a clear path on the northern side of the hill that permits travellers to get quite near the monument atop Amon Firn. You should travel to the location described by the journal, and read the appropriate pages while you are there.\n8\tConsider the image of King Artandil\tNarndir's writing has brought important figures of Cardolan's past to your imagination at the site of the Battle of the Deadmount, Amon Firn.\n9\tConsider the image of Amondir, Lord of Tyrn Gorthad\tNarndir's writing has brought important figures of Cardolan's past to your imagination at the site of the Battle of the Deadmount, Amon Firn.\n10\tRead Narndir's journal while in the south-eastern reaches of Tyrn Gorthad\tNarndir's journal describes a location in the south-eastern reaches of Tyrn Gorthad. You should travel to the location described by the journal, and read the appropriate pages while you are there.\n11\tConsider the image of the Witch-king\tNarndir's writing speaks of terrible deeds done by forces of great evil among the barrows of Tyrn Gorthad.\n12\tConsider the image of Amondir\tNarndir's writing speaks of terrible deeds done by forces of great evil among the barrows of Tyrn Gorthad.\n13\tWitness Prince Amondir's final adventure\tNarndir's writing speaks of terrible deeds done by forces of great evil among the barrows of Tyrn Gorthad.\n14\tTalk to Meneldir in the south-eastern reaches of Tyrn Gorthad\tMeneldir stands nearby, gazing out at the barrows of Tyrn Gorthad.\n",
[2092]="70000103\n1\tTalk to Aragorn in Rivendell\tAragorn can be found in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House in Rivendell, which lies in the Trollshaws. Halbarad has asked you to take word of the invasion of the North Downs to his chieftain, Aragorn, and to obtain his advice.\n",
[2093]="70042DEE\n1\tTalk to Derufin among the Osgiliath Culverts and go with him to search for Grond\tDerufin can be found among the Osgiliath Culverts beneath the city. Damrod has asked you and Derufin to find the great ram, Grond, and damage or destroy it before it is pulled out of Osgiliath into the Pelennor.\n2\tTalk to Derufin among the Osgiliath Culverts\tYou managed to damage Grond, but learned an unsettling truth about the identity of Gothmog, a commander of the forces in Osgiliath.\n3\tTalk to Damrod among the Osgiliath Culverts\tDamrod is with his men among the culverts beneath Osgiliath.\n",
[2094]="70061C8F\n1\tTalk to Handarod at Sírlond\tHandarod is at Sírlond, the Elf-camp across the river from Caranost. Meneldir wonders if Handarod might know what happened to the missing pages of Narndir's journal.\n2\tSearch the strange square ruin beside the road in Ruddymore where Handarod once saw Narndir acting strangely\tHandarod once saw Narndir acting strangely near the lone square ruin beside the road in Ruddymore, north-west of Herne.\n3\tOpen the small wooden box and search for the missing pages of Narndir's journal\tYou may have found another secret cache of Narndir's, but it is possible that Orcs or their allies found it first.\n4\tCollect the missing pages of Narndir's journal from Orcs, half-orcs, or goblins in the South Downs or Ruddymore (total: 6)\tOrcs, half-orcs, or goblins throughout the South Downs or Ruddymore may have stolen the missing pages of Narndir's journal, and you should recover them if you can.\n5\tReassemble Narndir's journal at the table at Scurloc Farm\tThe table at Scurloc Farm will be a suitable workspace for reassembling Narndir's journal.\n6\tRead Narndir's restored journal\tYou have restored Narndir's journal, and perhaps now you can learn why pages were removed from it.\n7\tShow Narndir's journal to Meneldir just south of Dol Ernil, in Tyrn Gorthad\tMeneldir told you he would meet up with you at outside Dol Ernil after you learned what you could from Narndir's journal.\n8\tRead Narndir's journal while by the throne in Dol Ernil\tNarndir's journal describes the throne room of Dol Ernil, located north of the Ranger Gorwen's camp-site and up some flights of stairs. You should travel to the location described by the journal, and read the appropriate pages while you are there.\n9\tConsider the image of the Grey Fear\tNarndir's writing has conjured the sight of the Grey Fear to trouble your mind.\n10\tConsider the death of Ostir, Last Prince of Cardolan, as described in the writings of Narndir\tNarndir describes the death of Ostir, Last Prince of Cardolan, with such detail that the account would pain any friend of the Dúnedain or their folk.\n11\tBring Narndir's journal to Meneldir at Gorwen's camp south of Dol Ernil\tMeneldir is waiting at Gorwen's camp south of Dol Ernil for you to return from your investigation inside the keep.\n",
[2095]="70061C9F\n1\tTalk to Gorwen at her camp south of Dol Ernil, in Tyrn Gorthad\tGorwen is at her camp south of Dol Ernil, in Tyrn Gorthad. Meneldir asked you to see what help Gorwen needs to combat the evils of Tyrn Gorthad.\n2\tDefeat wights in Tyrn Gorthad (total: 10)\030Defeat crebain, crawlers, or gaunt-men in Tyrn Gorthad (total: 8)\030Collect ancient swords among the ruins in Tyrn Gorthad (total: 4)\tGorwen gave you a number of tasks that will help her combat the evils of Tyrn Gorthad.\n3\tTalk to Gorwen at her camp south of Dol Ernil, in Tyrn Gorthad\tGorwen awaits your return at her camp south of Dol Ernil, in Tyrn Gorthad.\n4\tTalk to Meneldir at Gorwen's camp south of Dol Ernil\tMeneldir is at Gorwen's camp south of Dol Ernil, interested to hear of your accomplishments throughout Tyrn Gorthad.\n5\tBring the ancient swords to Halbarad so they may be destroyed\tHalbarad is at Sarn Ford. Meneldir asked you to bring the ancient swords you recovered to Halbarad so they can be destroyed and their evil diminished.\n6\tReturn to Gorwen's camp south of Dol Ernil, in Tyrn Gorthad\tHalbarad suggested that the two of you return to Gorwen's camp south of Dol Ernil.\n7\tTalk to Halbarad at Gorwen's camp south of Dol Ernil\tHalbarad and some of his company have come to Gorwen's camp in Tyrn Gorthad, but both Meneldir and Gorwen have already vanished. Have they gone to face the evil alone?\n",
[2096]="70000104\n1\tTalk to Candaith\tTravel along the road to the west until you reach The Forsaken Inn. Candaith is at a camp north of The Forsaken Inn, north-west of Weathertop. Frideric told you that a Ranger desires to speak with you about urgent matters.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad is in the North Downs, north of Meluinen. Candaith's fellow Ranger is in urgent need of assistance.\n",
[2097]="70027AB9\n1\tTalk to Nona in the Starkmoor\tNona is by the farmhouse in the north-western reaches of Starkmoor. Nona has agreed to meet you in the Starkmoor to scout for the information Lheu Brenin needs.\n2\tScout the farmhouse atop the north-western hill\030Scout the sheep-enclosure\030Scout the planted field\tThere is a farmhouse in the north-western corner of the Starkmoor. Nona wants you to scout the farmhouse atop the slope to the west to see if it is held by those loyal to Saruman.\n3\tTalk to Nona in the Starkmoor\tNona is by the farmland in the north-western reaches of the Starkmoor. You scouted the farmland in the north-western Starkmoor and should speak with Nona.\n",
[2098]="700442B7\n1\tThe city of Minas Tirith is besieged, and the forces of Mordor assault the wall. To participate in the defence, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Defence of Minas Tirith' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.\t\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir in the besieged city, at the south-eastern area of the Second Circle\tMithrandir is in the besieged city, at the south-eastern area of the Second Circle. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n",
[2099]="700442BF\n1\tThe city of Minas Tirith is besieged, and the great ram Grond creeps closer to the gate. To participate in the defence, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Hammer of the Underworld' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.\t\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir in the besieged city, at the south-eastern area of the Second Circle\tMithrandir is in the besieged city, at the south-eastern area of the Second Circle. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n",
[2100]="70027ABA\n1\tHelp the people of the Starkmoor as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Nona by the road into Dunbog\tNona is along the road that runs south out of the Starkmoor into the Dunbog, near a natural arch of stone. Nona has asked you to help the people of the Starkmoor with their problems, especially at Avardin to the south, and to meet her by the road into the Dunbog when you are satisfied.\n",
[2101]="70027ACA\n1\tDetermine whether the scout by the rocky outcropping is friendly\030Scout the small camp of Dunlendings south-west of the rocky outcropping\tA Dunlending-scout is by the large rocky outcropping that stands by the entrance to the Dunbog, and to the south-west of her is a small camp belonging to her people.\n2\tTalk to Nona in the Dunbog\tNona is to the north of the rocky outcropping that marks the boundary between the Starkmoor and the Dunbog. You have scouted the border of the Dunbog and should return to Nona.\n",
[2102]="700442C1\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir in the besieged city and travel with him to the gate\tMithrandir is in the besieged city, at the south-eastern area of the Second Circle. Grond has broken the gate, and now Mithrandir seeks to confront the Witch-king before that terrible foe can enter the city. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n2\tTalk to Peregrin Took at his post in the Seventh Circle\tPeregrin Took is in the Seventh Circle of the city, at his post. You have shaken away the remnants of the terrible prophecy Denethor spoke to you, but you cannot forget the images his words raised in your mind. To convince yourself that it was simply a tale, you should find Peregrin and ensure he is well.\n",
[2103]="70027ACB\n1\tHelp the people of Dunbog as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Nona in Carreglyn\tYou should help the people of the Dunbog with their worries, then meet up with Nona in the town of Barnavon, in Carreglyn, when you are satisfied.\n",
[2104]="700442C3\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir in the Court of the Fountain\tMithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain on the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith. Peregrin Took has suggested that you tell Mithrandir about your audience with Denethor, the Steward of Gondor.\n",
[2105]="70027ACC\n1\tCollect bribing gold from hostile Dunlendings in Carreglyn (total: 6)\tHostile Dunlendings in Barnavon carry the gold with which they were bribed. Nona wants you to defeat hostile Dunlendings throughout Carreglyn, but especially in the upper village of Barnavon, and take the bribing gold from them.\n2\tBring the bribing gold to Nona\tNona is in the village of Barnavon, in Carreglyn. You have retrieved the bribing gold and should bring it to Nona.\n",
[2106]="70027AD1\n1\tHelp the people of Carreglyn as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Amlan on the western border of Gravenwood\tThe Ranger Amlan is east of Carreglyn, just over the border with Gravenwood. Nona wants you to help the friendly people of Carreglyn as much as you can and to then meet up with the Rangers in Gravenwood when you are satisfied.\n2\tTalk to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp\tSaeradan is at the Rohirrim Scout-camp, east of Amlan's camp in Gravenwood. Amlan told you that a small party of Rohirrim have come to Gravenwood and are meeting with Saeradan.\n3\tTalk to Théodred at the Rohirrim scout-camp\tThéodred is at the Rohirrim scout-camp in Gravenwood. You have encountered Saeradan again and he has introduced you to Théodred, the son of the king of Rohan.\n",
[2107]="70027ADD\n1\tCheck near the mustering tree for signs of a watchful presence\030Check in the back of Uvel-cadlus for signs of a watchful presence\tThéodred's men have felt the watchful presence at an old tree to the north-west of his camp, and in the back of Uvel-cadlus, the Dragon-clan camp to the north. Théodred wants you to see if you can sense a watchful presence at the places his men experienced such feelings.\n2\tTalk to Théodred at the Rohirrim scout-camp\tThéodred is at his camp in the eastern reaches of Gravenwood. You have sought out the watchful presence in Gravenwood, but did not experience anything unusual.\n",
[2108]="70027ADE\n1\tHelp the people of the Gravenwood as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, report to Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva\tYou should help Théodred's men deal with the mysteries of the Gravenwood before returning to Lheu Brenin with what you have learned in Dunland.\n",
[2109]="70027ADF\n1\tTalk to Lheu Brenin and travel with him to speak with the captive\tLheu Brenin is outside his home in Tûr Morva. Lheu Brenin has asked you to come with him to speak with his captive.\n2\tTalk to Fâsh in Isengard\tIf you left the Isengard Depths without the Reminder of Captivity in your inventory, go to the cart just to the right of the gate of Isengard and use it to return to the Depths. You have been taken prisoner and brought to Isengard. The Falcon-clan has betrayed you, and you are now the prisoner of Saruman.\n",
[2110]="70027B01\n1\tFâsh has assigned an Uruk-hai to keep an eye on you in the caverns beneath Isengard and to give you work. If your overseer wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.\t\n2\tFâsh has assigned an Uruk-hai to keep an eye on you in the caverns beneath Isengard and to give you work. If your overseer wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.\t\n3\tFâsh has assigned an Uruk-hai to keep an eye on you in the caverns beneath Isengard and to give you work. If your overseer wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.\t\n4\tReturn to Fâsh in the centre of the caverns\tFâsh is in the centre of the caverns beneath Isengard. You have finished a series of tasks for your Uruk-hai overseer and should return to Fâsh.\n",
[2111]="700145B5\n1\tAid Slóthi with his preparations\030Aid Sigdan with his preparations\030Aid Thálfi with his preparations\tThe dwarves Slóthi, Sigdan, and Thálfi are in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. Bósi fears that war may be coming, and he wants the defences of the Great Delving made ready.\n2\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance of Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. You have helped with the preparations to make the Great Delving ready for war and should report now to Bósi.\n",
[2112]="70044269\n1\tTalk to Duilin outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern end of the Pelennor Fields\tDuilin is outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern side of the Pelennor Fields. Osgiliath has fallen to the enemy, and the men there can no longer mount an effective resistance.\n2\tDefeat foes on the Pelennor Fields (total: 8)\030Check fallen soldier\tThe safety of Minas Tirith is threatened by the foes that have come to the Pelennor Fields. Men fled from the occupation of the Causeway Forts and fell not far from Osgiliath. Duilin and Derufin have asked you to search for survivors injured while fleeing from the Causeway Forts, and to defeat foes on the Pelennor.\n3\tTalk to Duilin outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern end of the Pelennor Fields\tDuilin and Derufin are outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern side of the Pelennor Fields.\n4\tTalk to Derufin outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern end of the Pelennor Fields\tDuilin and Derufin are outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern side of the Pelennor Fields.\n",
})
